Back to the budget-only portfolio. $L = \mathbf{w}^T oldsymbol{\Sigma}\mathbf{w} + 
u(1 - \mathbf{1}^T\mathbf{w})$ is lowest at $\mathbf{w} = 	frac{
u}{2} oldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1}\mathbf{1}$. That gives $g(
u) = 
u - 	frac{
u^2}{4}s$, with $s = \mathbf{1}^T oldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1}\mathbf{1} = 	frac{1525}{36} \approx 42.3611$. Drag along $g$.
